※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4495

※ `#` answers how many things something is made of.  A value that is one thing
※ is not made of a number of things, and answering one for it would be
※ answering a question nobody asked.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 5u8
    let how_many: u64 = #n
    0u6
